From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:00:53 +0800
Subject: Top panel: keep the layer-shell exclusive zone equal to the panel
 thickness

Android cutout metadata can change the top panel's thickness after its first Wayland configure.
Resizing the visible panel alone left the original exclusive zone, so applications kept the old
reserved area. The panel now sets its layer-shell exclusion zone to its real thickness whenever
the thickness, visibility mode or floating state changes.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [a thickness change after the first configure is not Android specific; check upstream master first]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:display.geometry
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/43
---
 shell/contents/views/Panel.qml | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/shell/contents/views/Panel.qml b/shell/contents/views/Panel.qml
index fc195a8..7672d1f 100644
--- a/shell/contents/views/Panel.qml
+++ b/shell/contents/views/Panel.qml
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ import org.kde.taskmanager 0.1 as TaskManager
 import org.kde.kwindowsystem 1.0
 import org.kde.kirigami as Kirigami
 import org.kde.plasma.shell.panel 0.1 as Panel
+import org.kde.layershell 1.0 as LayerShell
 
 import org.kde.plasma.plasmoid 2.0
 
@@ -33,6 +34,25 @@ Item {
         }
     }
 
+    // Android cutout metadata can change the top panel thickness after its
+    // initial Wayland configure. Keep the reserved application area in sync;
+    // resizing the visible panel alone can leave the original exclusive zone.
+    // Use the real (integer) PanelView thickness, not a second safe-area margin.
+    function syncTopPanelExclusion() {
+        if (containment?.plasmoid?.location === PlasmaCore.Types.TopEdge
+                && panel.visibilityMode === Panel.Global.NormalPanel
+                && !panel.floating) {
+            panel.LayerShell.Window.exclusionZone = panel.thickness;
+            panel.requestUpdate();
+        }
+    }
+    Component.onCompleted: Qt.callLater(root.syncTopPanelExclusion)
+    Connections {
+        target: panel
+        function onThicknessChanged() { Qt.callLater(root.syncTopPanelExclusion); }
+        function onVisibilityModeChanged() { Qt.callLater(root.syncTopPanelExclusion); }
+    }
+
     // NOTE: Below is taken straight out of Plasma Desktop so that we can
     //       support desktop panels properly, try to keep it in sync:
     //       plasma-desktop/desktoppackage/contents/views/Panel.qml
